course: dictionary
lesson: 11636
title: Words about numbers
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Arithmetic is the maths of numbers: adding, subtracting, multiplying and dividing. Arithmetical is the describing word for it. It tells you a thing is about arithmetic. «Her arithmetical skills helped her check the shopping bill.» Here, skills are about adding and subtracting numbers.
explain: Look for the clue in the word itself. Arithmetic is the noun, and arithmetical is the adjective. Adjectives describe nouns, so in «an arithmetical mistake», the word arithmetical tells you what kind of mistake it is: a mistake with numbers.
explain: Maths books use this word in phrases you will meet often. «He made an arithmetical error: 7 + 5 is 12, not 13.» An arithmetical sequence is a list of numbers that goes up by the same amount each time. Ask yourself: what is going up, and by how much?
fact: Arithmetical means about arithmetic: adding, subtracting, multiplying and dividing numbers.
fact: «Arithmetical error» means a mistake when working with numbers.
fact: «Arithmetical progression» means a list of numbers that goes up, or down, by the same amount each time, such as 2, 4, 6, 8.
fact: Arithmetical is an adjective, so it describes a noun such as skill, mistake or sequence.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence: if the sentence is about numbers, arithmetical probably fits.
exercise: «Her arithmetical skills helped her check the shopping bill.» What does arithmetical mean here? | About the weather | *About adding and subtracting numbers | About animals | Drawing pictures
exercise: «He made an arithmetical error: 7 + 5 is 12, not 13.» What is an arithmetical error? | *A mistake with the numbers in a sum | A picture that is drawn too big | A spelling mistake in a story | A late bus
exercise: The numbers 3, 6, 9, 12 form an arithmetical sequence. Which numbers come next? | 10, 20, 30 | *15, 18, 21 | 16, 20, 24 | 12, 14, 16
test: What does «arithmetical progression» mean? | *Numbers that go up by the same amount each time | Writing poems | Painting a sunset | Singing songs in a choir
test: Which skill is arithmetical? | Reading a poem aloud | Singing a song | Drawing a map | *Dividing 20 by 4
exam: Which question is an arithmetical question? | Describe a cat | Tell a joke | Name your favourite colour | *What is 8 multiplied by 3?
